    <text>
        <front>
            <div type="summary">
                <p>
                    Vanessa Bell, at the request of Leonard Woolf, asks that formal corrections be made to the book layout of a collection of texts by Virginia Woolf, The Death of the Moth and Other Essays, specifically regarding the layout of the dustjacket.
                </p>
            </div>
        </front>
        <body>
            <div type="letter">
                <opener>
                    <dateline>
                        <date when="1942-04-14">
                            <choice>
                                <abbr>Ap.</abbr>
                                <expan>April</expan>
                            </choice> 14
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                    <salute>
                        Dear John
                    </salute>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    Leonard <note><p>Vanessa Bell refers here to <persName key="Q703935">Leonard Woolf</persName>, <persName key="Q40909">Virginia Woolf</persName>'s husband.</p></note> asks me to return this directly <lb/>
                    to you &amp; to tell you that it must <lb/>
                    be <title>THE death of the Moth</title> <note><p>The Death of the Moth, and Other Essays is a collection of essays written by Virginia Woolf, published posthumously in 1942, one year after its author's suicide.</p></note>. Also <lb/>
                    that &quot;and other essays&quot; must be deleted. <lb/>
                    I prefer A to B. &quot;Death of the Moth&quot; <lb/>
                    must be lower, the bottom line of the <lb/>
                    letters to come where the smaller letters <lb/>
                    now come &amp; THE must be put in <lb/>
                    the centre above in the smaller type<supplied>.</supplied> <lb/>
                    Also the name at the bottom I think <lb/>
                    should be a tiny bit lower, so as to be <lb/>
                    more on a level with the drawing. I <lb/>
                    have marked the place in pencil. <lb/>
                    I think it should be in the blackest <lb/>
                    ink on the whitest paper possible.
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>Your Vanessa</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
